properties.description:
Ten tests.

drain.rs, seven, against a fake service over a real listener:
- a request is work until its answer's body is done, and a GET never is;
- an answer dropped unread stops counting;
- waiting ends when the work does, or at the deadline;
- a request in progress when the stop comes is answered in full (to the chunked body's closing chunk) and its connection closes after it;
- work that outlasts the grace is cut off, the stop stays bounded, and the report says "cut off";
- an open stream (a GET that never ends) does not make the stop wait out a 30 s grace;
- durations read back the way the flags take them.

registry_http.rs, one: a stopping router closes every design, every store is released, and a request after that is Busy (503).

End to end, two, over the real binary and a real SIGTERM:
- a --http --export-to server written to inside the write-through's two-second quiet period exits 0, the export contains the write, stderr says "stopped (SIGTERM)" and "every store released cleanly", and the store reopens with the change in it;
- a --registry-root server with two open designs exits 0 and names each design it closed.
